Azure architecture icons — Microsoft Corporation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:   src/icons-azure.generated.json
         (and the copies of it in any built artifact: dist/, the npm package,
         and the desktop installers)

Source:  https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/architecture/icons/
         "Azure Public Service Icons" V24, converted to Iconify format by
         scripts/build-azure-icons.mjs. The artwork is unmodified: the
         conversion changes the container, not the drawings.

These icons are Microsoft's. They are NOT licensed under Archyne's MIT
licence, and no permission over them is granted by it. Microsoft's terms, in
full, as published on the page above:

    "Microsoft permits the use of these icons in architectural diagrams,
     training materials, or documentation. You can copy, distribute, and
     display the icons only for the permitted use unless granted explicit
     permission by Microsoft. Microsoft reserves all other rights."

And Microsoft's guidance for using them:

    Do   - use the icons to illustrate how products work together
    Do   - include the product name near the icon in a diagram
    Do   - use the icons as they appear within Azure
    Don't- crop, flip, rotate, distort or otherwise change an icon's shape
    Don't- use Microsoft product icons to represent your product or service

Archyne bundles them so that architecture diagrams can be drawn with the
icons the subject matter actually has: Iconify's 231 collections contain no
Azure set, and without these there is no icon for a virtual network, a subnet
or a Key Vault. They are shipped for use in diagrams — the permitted use —
and Archyne does not use them as its own branding, in its interface chrome,
or to represent Archyne itself.

If Microsoft would prefer this pack were not distributed with Archyne, please
open an issue at https://github.com/dariodd/archyne/issues and it will be
removed promptly: it is one generated file and one loader entry, and every
icon remains importable by the user from Microsoft's own download.

